      "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef main():\n    # Load without modifying original memmap; convert to float32 array for BLAS speed\n    X = np.load('vectors.npy')\n    if X.dtype != np.float32:\n        X = X.astype(np.float32)\n    n = X.shape[0]\n\n    # Precompute squared norms in float64 for accuracy\n    sq = np.einsum('ij,ij->i', X, X, dtype=np.float64)\n\n    total = 0.0\n    chunk = 512  # balance between BLAS efficiency and memory usage\n\n    for i0 in range(0, n, chunk):\n        i1 = min(i0 + chunk, n)\n        Xi = X[i0:i1]                # (rows, d)\n        Xj = X[i0:n]                 # (cols, d), cols = n - i0\n\n        # Gram matrix block: rows x cols\n        G = Xi @ Xj.T                # float32 matmul via BLAS\n        G = G.astype(np.float64)\n\n        sqi = sq[i0:i1][:, None]\n        sqj = sq[i0:n][None, :]\n\n        d2 = sqi + sqj - 2.0 * G\n        np.maximum(d2, 0.0, out=d2)\n        np.sqrt(d2, out=d2)\n\n        rows_local = np.arange(i1 - i0)[:, None]\n        cols_local = np.arange(n - i0)[None, :]\n        mask = cols_local > rows_local  # strictly upper part (j > i in global indices)\n\n        total += d2[mask].sum()\n\n    total *= 2.0  # account for both (i,j) and (j,i); diagonal is zero, unaffected\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total}\")\n\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    main()\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
